# Vchat Configuration

This file contains helpful information for developers.

## Environment Variables

No environment variables are needed! Everything runs client-side.

## Puter.js Configuration

The app uses Puter.js with default settings:
- Authentication via Puter OAuth
- KV Store for chat persistence
- AI APIs for chat and image generation

## Browser Compatibility

- ✅ Chrome/Edge (v90+)
- ✅ Firefox (v88+)
- ✅ Safari (v14+)
- ✅ Mobile browsers (iOS Safari, Chrome Mobile)

## Development

### Run locally:
```bash
python3 -m http.server 8000
# Visit http://localhost:8000
```

### Or use Node.js:
```bash
npx http-server -p 8000
```

### Or use VS Code Live Server:
Right-click `index.html` → "Open with Live Server"

## API Endpoints Used

All APIs are provided by Puter.js:
- `puter.auth.*` - Authentication
- `puter.ai.chat()` - AI chat
- `puter.ai.txt2img()` - Image generation
- `puter.kv.*` - Key-value storage

No backend server required!

## Storage

Chat history is stored in Puter's KV store under the key:
- `vchat_history` - Contains all user chats as JSON

## Customization

### Change Colors:
Edit CSS variables in `styles.css`:
```css
:root {
    --primary: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
    /* ... more variables */
}
```

### Add Features:
The app is modular. Check `app.js` for all available functions.

## Security

- ✅ All authentication handled by Puter
- ✅ No sensitive data stored locally
- ✅ HTTPS required (automatic on GitHub Pages)
- ✅ No API keys needed in code

## Performance

- 📦 Total size: ~50KB (uncompressed)
- ⚡ No build step required
- 🚀 Fast loading with CDN-hosted Puter.js
- 💾 Efficient local storage with KV store
